# {{ repo.folder }}

GitOps repository for **{{ project.name }}**. It holds desired deployed state only; Argo CD
syncs it into the cluster. Generated by [plinth](https://github.com/dfoshidero/plinth).

## Layout

```
{{ defaults.CONFIG_FILENAME }}                  the project's plinth config (used by plinth add / update)
bootstrap/root.yaml          app-of-apps: point Argo CD here once
apps/project.yaml            Argo CD project scoping repos and namespaces
apps/<env>.yaml              one ApplicationSet per environment
charts/workload/             Helm chart that deploys a Score workload
environments/<env>/<workload>/
  values.yaml                per-environment overrides (replicas, ...)
  release.yaml               written by CI: image, app revision, score path
```

Environments: {{ config.environments | join(", ") }}. Each deploys into namespace `{{ project.name }}-<env>`.

An ApplicationSet creates one Argo CD Application per `release.yaml` it finds. Each Application
renders `charts/workload` with the workload's `score.yaml` (read from its app repo at the released
commit) plus this repo's `values.yaml`, and the released image. Deleting a `release.yaml` removes
that Application and everything it deployed.

