## Releasing and promoting

CI in each app repo writes `environments/{{ defaults.RELEASE_ENVIRONMENT }}/<workload>/release.yaml` on every
push to main, so `{{ defaults.RELEASE_ENVIRONMENT }}` always runs the latest build. To promote, copy that file to
another environment and merge it:

{% set example = plan.workloads()[0][1].name %}
{% set promote_to = config.environments | reject("equalto", defaults.RELEASE_ENVIRONMENT) | first | default("staging") %}
```sh
cp environments/{{ defaults.RELEASE_ENVIRONMENT }}/{{ example }}/release.yaml environments/{{ promote_to }}/{{ example }}/release.yaml
```

Nothing deploys to an environment until its `release.yaml` exists.

## Run it locally

Needs Docker, [k3d](https://k3d.io), kubectl and Helm. Push this repo and the app repos first,
and let CI ship once so there are images to deploy:

```sh
# only needed for private repositories / images
export GIT_USERNAME=... GIT_TOKEN=...                 # read access to {{ project.git_base_url }}
export REGISTRY_USERNAME=... REGISTRY_PASSWORD=...    # pull access to {{ project.registry }}
./scripts/bootstrap-local.sh
```

This creates a k3d cluster, installs Argo CD (chart {{ defaults.ARGO_CD_CHART_VERSION }}), gives it the
credentials above (`{{ defaults.REPO_CREDS_SECRET }}` in `argocd`, `{{ defaults.IMAGE_PULL_SECRET }}` in each
environment's namespace) and applies `bootstrap/root.yaml`.

## Changing the project

Run plinth from the folder holding this repository and the app repositories:

```sh
plinth add service NAME     # or: plinth add worker NAME
plinth update               # merge the latest plinth templates into every repository
```
